re to integrate, monitor, or analyze data from multiple business operations within a unified system.\"","~A76~":"\"locator\"","~A77~":"\"transfers_proficiency\"","~A78~":"\"f16cc97a-5a3a-552c-b694-9a5a6c06362c\"","~A79~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Network configuration, connectivity and troubleshooting; infrastructure operations and architecture are distinct source scopes.\"","~A80~":"\"Software to connect different business systems to improve scalability or streamline work flows.\"","~A81~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Reproducible ingestion, transformation, storage and operation of data pipelines; generic software/database architecture is broader than this career.\"","~A82~":"\"Software to protect sensitive information, ensure the safe transfer of data, or detect or remove malware or computer viruses.\"","~A83~":"\"Software to support or run applications which provide services through a communication protocol.\"","~A84~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Build/test automation, deployment, containers and observability; software development, administration and platform roles are related, not a unique equivalent occupation.\"","~A85~":"\"Software to control, create, manage, or record the physical or functional characteristics of hardware or software.\"","~A86~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Microcontroller software, interfaces and hardware integration; generic software/hardware occupations are complementary and senior architecture duties remain separate.\"","~A87~":"\"Software to present, visualize, or analyze data to help businesses make informed decisions.\"","~A88~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Question framing, data preparation, analysis and communication; data-science and engineering references are complementary, not equivalent roles.\"","~A89~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Prediction framing, model training/evaluation and reproducible inference; senior data-science and generic software roles are related references.\"","~A90~":"\"Software to isolate business logic in programs from platform-specific code, so each can be maintained independently. May provide transaction management, clustering, failover, or load balancing.\"","~A91~":"\"proposed_partial_coverage\"","~A92~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Visual interface hierarchy, components, responsive states and design handoff; broad interface occupations include tasks outside this career.\"","~A93~":"\"functional_competency\"","~A94~":"\"Software to monitor, analyze, or detect network systems.\"","~A95~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Research, synthesis, flows, prototyping and usability evidence; UI and UX remain distinct despite a shared O*NET occupation.\"","~A96~":"\"Software to draw or manipulate images. May adjust colors, add text, or apply special effects.\"","~A97~":"\"work_activities\"","~A98~":"\"Software to manage computers, peripherals, or printers connected to a network. May detect new hardware or install software on connected devices.\"","~A99~":"\"competency_ids\"","~A100~":"\"Software to produce summaries or visualizations of raw data stored in a database system.\"","~A101~":"\"41757b82-ed33-5bf7-acb6-6ec82f8e25b1\"","~A102~":"\"native_task_code\"","~A103~":"\"c6e2f328-7b30-5d0f-a226-61db07fe1314\"","~A104~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Explicitly authorized assessment, safe validation and remediation reporting; manager duties and conflicting levels do not define analyst thresholds.\"","~A105~":"\"Research, design, and develop computer and network software or specialized utility programs. Analyze user needs and develop software solutions, applying principles and techniques of computer science, engineering, and mathematical analysis. Update software or enhance existing software capabilities. May work with computer hardware engineers to integrate hardware and software systems, and develop specifications and performance requirements. May maintain databases within an application area, working individually or coordinating database development as part of a team.\"","~A106~":"\"Pending source-specific reuse/attribution review; download availability is not permission to redistribute.\"","~A107~":"\"transferable_skills\"","~A108~":"\"f9761b0b52be1828b38a3e5e0ae59a93a7b0ce358bc800f52f57a8b002adeb3e\"","~A109~":"\"https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco/download/privacy-statement\"","~A110~":"\"Software to manage hybrid, private, or public cloud-based systems and infrastructure.\"","~A111~":"\"Software to design 2D or 3D objects. May include engineering or architectural features.\"","~A112~":"\"Design digital user interfaces or websites. Develop and test layouts, interfaces, functionality, and navigation menus to ensure compatibility and usability across browsers or devices. May use web framework applications as well as client-side code and processes. May evaluate web design following web and accessibility standards, and may analyze web use metrics and optimize websites for marketability and search engine ranking. May design and test interfaces that facilitate the human-computer interaction and maximize the usability of digital devices, websites, and software with a focus on aesthetics and design. May create graphics used in websites and manage website content and links.\"","~A113~":"\"1878d764-8f92-5a5b-bc2c-94a91cd61ec7\"","~A114~":"\"Software to manage or store \\\"data about data\\\" such as author, creation date, file size, or keywords.\"","~A115~":"\"012d408d-f5f8-5b75-a486-72f6dfe4b2ae\"","~A116~":"\"73d6bc81-3182-5494-a870-5883eceb995a\"","~A117~":"\"Software to share or co-author computer files through cloud computing, where documents are stored in a central \\\"cloud\\\" of networked servers.\"","~A118~":"\"Software to plan, organize, staff, or control the completion of a product or set of tasks.\"","~A119~":"\"1b3ee503-2a6b-5fbd-847a-444edf2f8b5a\"","~A120~":"\"Software to back up information from computer systems to additional destinations such as networked servers or tape drives.\"","~A121~":"\"Knowledge of the chemical composition, structure, and properties of substances and of the chemical processes and transformations that they undergo. This includes uses of chemicals and their interactions, danger signs, production techniques, and disposal methods.\"","~A122~":"\"Software to create, manage, or monitor product development processes to comply with standards, specifications, or risk management policies.\"","~A123~":"\"05592c78-1d12-57cc-834e-135b0dd18f01\"","~A124~":"\"Retain native task under its named source role; Low-voltage circuit and PCB design, review and testing; semiconductor circuit roles are narrower than the general career.\"","~A125~":"\"94481768-cbf7-5c84-aced-ecb6d7267d5b\"","~A126~":"\"f8577e8e-934d-504c-aff0-94f1babf89b9\"","~A127~":"\"Explicit agent scope selection: Microcontroller software, interfaces and hardware integration; generic software/hardware occupations are complementary and senior architecture duties remain separate.\"","~A128~":"\"Software to create or maintain applications which interact with users through a graphical interface.\"","~A129~":"\"006acb19-6cd3-5122-95db-6915580690fb\"","~A130~":"\"01d7d1e9-839c-5063-b1e2-1faef1c4a783\"","~A131~":"\"02a63dae-ad10-5469-aacb-2e40896d7eaf\"","~A132~":"\"06188921-bba5-586c-8cc2-88b6e9eee821\"","~A133~":"\"0d476aeb-51e8-5e89-bb31-8c6935e8c0c4\"","~A134~":"\"0dd4442f-5347-5747-94c5-e58e071b0cb7\"","~A135~":"\"186c67a3-c1c7-59f3-919f-562d4bb46f3f\"","~A136~":"\"19a36c0b-c6a6-5338-8f4b-d0d56546b42d\"","~A137~":"\"1b225a29-28d0-5034-8a5d-5df669433deb\"","~A138~":"\"1b4ef70b-079e-5a02-bf42-51f60775fc7a\"","~A139~":"\"1d9928ca-a0e7-5b4b-90f9-e63bd08c5a8d\"","~A140~":"\"1e458a35-fcac-5b49-bbaa-188992e81a1d\"","~A141~":"\"1e81a571-061b-5b67-831b-95e0bca77374\"","~A142~":"\"1eca4745-c036-5bd3-a286-20d568bd571d\"","~A143~":"\"2